#: includes/settings.php
msgid "General Settings"
msgstr "Ntọala Izugbe"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Syslog Enabled"
msgstr "Gbanyere Syslog"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "If this checkbox is set, records will be transferred from the Syslog Incoming table to the main syslog table and Alerts and Reports will be enabled.  Please keep in mind that if the system is disabled log entries will still accumulate into the Syslog Incoming table as this is defined by the rsyslog or syslog-ng process."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na edobere igbe nlele a, a ga-ebufe ndekọ site na tebụl Syslog Incoming gaa na tebụl syslog bụ isi ma gbanye Mkpu na Akụkọ.  Biko buru n'uche na ọ bụrụ na agbanyụrụ sistemụ, ndenye ndekọ ga-anọgide na-agbakọta na tebụl Syslog Incoming n'ihi na usoro rsyslog ma ọ bụ syslog-ng kọwapụtara nke a."

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Forward alarms to Alarm Manager"
msgstr "Ziga mkpu na Onye Njikwa Mkpu"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Allow rules set to Alarm Manager to forward alarms. Syslog email remains the fallback; command actions run only for Syslog Alarming rules."
msgstr "Kwe ka iwu ndị e debere na Njikwa Mkpu bufee mkpu. Ozi-e Syslog ka bụ nhọrọ ndabere; omume iwu na-arụ ọrụ naanị maka iwu Mkpu Syslog."

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Strip Domains"
msgstr "Wepụ Domini Gasị"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "A comma delimited list of domains that you wish to remove from the syslog hostname, Examples would be 'mydomain.com, otherdomain.com'"
msgstr "Ndepụta ngalaba nke rịkọm kewara nke ị chọrọ iwepụ na aha onye nnabata Syslog, ọmụmaatụ ga-abụ 'mydomain.com, otherdomain.com'"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Refresh Interval"
msgstr "Oge Mmelite"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "This is the time in seconds before the page refreshes."
msgstr "Nke a bụ oge n'ime sekọnd tupu peeji ahụ emegharịa."

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Skip Total Row Count"
msgstr "Wụfee Ngụkọta Ahịrị Niile"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "If this checkbox is set, the System Logs and Alert Logs tabs do not count every matching record, which can be very expensive on large installations. The page shows Previous and Next links instead of a total and page list, and Next is offered while more records remain."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na edobere igbe nlele a, taabụ Ndekọ Sistemụ na Ndekọ Mkpu anaghị agụ ndekọ ọ bụla dakọtara, nke nwere ike ịdị oke ọnụ na nrụnye buru ibu. Ibe ahụ na-egosi njikọ Nke Gara Aga na Nke Na-abịa kama ngụkọta na ndepụta ibe, a na-enyekwa Nke Na-abịa mgbe ndekọ ndị ọzọ ka dị."

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Max Report Records"
msgstr "Ndekọ Akụkọ Kacha Elu"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "For Threshold based Alerts, what is the maximum number that you wish to show in the report.  This is used to limit the size of the html log and Email."
msgstr "Maka Mkpu ndị dabere na Ọnụ ụzọ, gịnị bụ ọnụọgụ kachasị ị chọrọ igosi na mkpesa ahụ.  A na-eji nke a egbochi oke nha nke ndekọ html na Ozi-e."

#: includes/settings.php
#, php-format
msgid "%d Records"
msgstr "%d Ndekọ"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Maximum Syslog Processing Processes"
msgstr "Usoro Nhazi Syslog Kacha Elu"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "When set above 1, incoming message processing is spread across parallel worker processes.  Each worker handles a disjoint range of incoming messages, speeding up hostname resolution and message transfer under heavy loads.  A setting of 1 processes all messages in a single process.  Worker processes are not supported on Windows or when the PHP pcntl and POSIX extensions are unavailable, in which case processing falls back to a single process."
msgstr "Mgbe edobere ya karịa 1, a na-ekesa nhazi ozi na-abata n'ofe usoro ndị ọrụ yiri ibe ha. Onye ọrụ ọ bụla na-ahụ maka oke ozi dị iche iche na-abata, na-eme ka mkpebi aha onye nnabata na nbufe ozi dị ngwa n'okpuru ibu dị arọ. Ntọala nke 1 na-ahazi ozi niile n'otu usoro. A naghị akwado usoro ndị ọrụ na Windows ma ọ bụ mgbe mgbakwunye PHP pcntl na POSIX adịghị, n'ọnọdụ ahụ nhazi na-alaghachi n'otu usoro."

#: includes/settings.php
#, php-format
msgid "%d Worker Process"
msgstr "%d Usoro Ọrụ"

#: includes/settings.php
#, php-format
msgid "%d Worker Processes"
msgstr "%d Usoro Ọrụ"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Command for Opening Tickets"
msgstr "Iwu maka Imepe Tiketi"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "This command will be executed for opening Help Desk Tickets.  The command will be required to parse multiple input parameters as follows: <b>--alert-name</b>, <b>--severity</b>, <b>--hostlist</b>, <b>--message</b>.  The hostlist will be a comma delimited list of hosts impacted by the alert."
msgstr "A ga-eme iwu a maka imeghe Tiketi Ebe Enyemaka. A ga-achọ ka iwu ahụ tụọ ọtụtụ paramita ntinye dị ka ndị a: <b>--alert-name</b>, <b>--severity</b>, <b>--hostlist</b>, <b>--message</b>. Ndepụta hostlist ga-abụ ndepụta ndị nnabata nke mkpọpu okwu (comma) kewara nke ọkwa ahụ metụtara."

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Host Discovery Options"
msgstr "Nhọrọ Nchọpụta Onye nnabata"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Enable Hostname Resolution"
msgstr "Gbanye Mkpebi Aha Onye Nnabata"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "If this checkbox is set, all hostnames are resolved via DNS lookup first (If enabled), using A and AAAA records. IPv4 and IPv6 addresses need no lookup, and IPv6 addresses are stored in compressed lower case form. If the DNS lookup fails, the system will attempt to resolve the hostname against the Cacti host table and replace it with the Cacti host description. If both DNS and Cacti lookups fail, records are assigned a prefix 'unresolved-Original_hostname'."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na edobere igbe nlele a, a ga-ebu ụzọ chọta aha ndị nnabata niile site na nchọta DNS (Ọ bụrụ na agbanyere ya), na-eji ndekọ A na AAAA. Adreesị IPv4 na IPv6 anaghị achọ nchọta, a na-echekwa adreesị IPv6 n'ụdị mkpụrụedemede nta a kpakọrọ akpakọ. Ọ bụrụ na nchọta DNS ada, sistemụ ahụ ga-anwa idozi aha onye nnabata megide tebụl onye nnabata Cacti ma jiri nkọwa onye nnabata Cacti dochie ya. Ọ bụrụ na nchọta DNS na Cacti daa, a na-ekenye ndekọ ahụ okwu mbido 'unresolved-Original_hostname'."

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Skip DNS Resolution for incoming hosts"
msgstr "Wụfee Mkpebi DNS maka ndị nnabata na-abata"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "If this checkbox is set, the system will not attempt to resolve hosts via DNS lookups.  This is useful for environments where DNS resolution is not possible or not desired."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na edobere igbe nlele a, sistemụ ahụ agaghị anwa ichọta ndị nnabata site na nchọta DNS.  Nke a bara uru maka gburugburu ebe nchọta DNS na-agaghị ekwe omume ma ọ bụ na achọghị ya."

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "HTML Notification Settings"
msgstr "Ntọala Ọkwa HTML"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Enable HTML Based Email"
msgstr "Gbanye Ozi-e Dabere na HTML"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "If this checkbox is set, all Emails will be sent in HTML format.  Otherwise, Emails will be sent in plain text."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na edobere igbe nlele a, a ga-ezipụ Ozi-e niile n'ụdị HTML.  Ma ọ bụghị ya, a ga-ezipụ Ozi-e n'ederede nkịtị."

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Format File to Use"
msgstr "Faịlụ Nhazi A Ga-eji"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Choose the custom html wrapper and CSS file to use.  This file contains both html and CSS to wrap around your report.  If it contains more than simply CSS, you need to place a special <REPORT> tag inside of the file.  This format tag will be replaced by the report content.  These files are located in the 'formats' directory."
msgstr "Họrọ faịlụ mkpuchi html ahaziri na CSS a ga-eji. Faịlụ a nwere ma html ma CSS iji kechie akụkọ gị. Ọ bụrụ na o nwere ihe karịrị naanị CSS, ị kwesịrị itinye mkpado <REPORT> pụrụ iche n'ime faịlụ ahụ. A ga-eji ọdịnaya akụkọ dochie mkpado nhazi a. Faịlụ ndị a dị na ndekọ 'formats'."

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Data Retention and Partitioning"
msgstr "Nchekwa Data na Nkewa"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Syslog Retention"
msgstr "Nchekwa Syslog"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "This is the number of days to keep events."
msgstr "Nke a bụ ọnụọgụgụ ụbọchị a ga-edobe ihe omume."

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "The size of each partition of the syslog and syslog_removed tables. A change is saved here but takes effect only when cli/upgrade_partitioning.php rebuilds both tables; until then, partition maintenance keeps the existing size. Hourly partitioning requires a finite retention. The retention, pre-create window and partitioning level together must fit the database server's partition limit, or the settings are not saved."
msgstr "Ogo nkewa nke ọ bụla nke tebụl syslog na syslog_removed. A na-echekwa mgbanwe ebe a mana ọ na-amalite ịrụ ọrụ naanị mgbe cli/upgrade_partitioning.php rụgharịrị tebụl abụọ ahụ; ruo mgbe ahụ, nlekọta nkewa na-edobe ogo dị ugbu a. Nkewa kwa awa chọrọ njigide nwere oke. Njigide, windo tupu e kee ya na ọkwa nkewa ọnụ ga-adabarịrị n'oke nkewa nke sava nchekwa data, maọbụ na a gaghị echekwa ntọala ndị ahụ."

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "Partition Pre-create Window"
msgstr "Oge Mbụ Maka Imepụta Nkewa"

#: includes/settings.php
msgid "This is the number of days of future partitions to maintain for partitioned Syslog tables, so that new partitions are always split from an empty dMaxValue partition.  Hourly partitioning always keeps at least 2 days."
msgstr "Nke a bụ ọnụọgụgụ ụbọchị nke nkewa ọdịnihu a ga-edobe maka tebụl Syslog e kewara ekewa, ka e wee na-ekewa nkewa ọhụrụ mgbe niile site na nkewa dMaxValue tọgbọrọ chakoo. Nkewa kwa elekere na-edobe ma ọ dịkarịa ala ụbọchị 2 mgbe niile."

