#: syslog_recommendations.php
msgid "The first 2,048 characters of the message are split into words. A word is a run of letters, digits and the characters _ . - / that may start with %. Every other character, such as a space, colon, comma or bracket, ends a word. In <code>%LINK-3-UPDOWN: Interface Gi0/1, changed state to down</code> the words are <code>%LINK-3-UPDOWN</code>, <code>Interface</code>, <code>Gi0/1</code>, <code>changed</code>, <code>state</code>, <code>to</code> and <code>down</code>."
msgstr "A na-ekewa mkpụrụedemede 2,048 mbụ nke ozi ahụ n'ime okwu. Okwu bụ usoro mkpụrụedemede, ọnụọgụgụ na akara _ . - / nke nwere ike iji % bido. Akara ọ bụla ọzọ, dị ka ohere, kọlọn, rịkọm ma ọ bụ nkwado, na-emecha okwu. Na <code>%LINK-3-UPDOWN: Interface Gi0/1, changed state to down</code> okwu ndị ahụ bụ <code>%LINK-3-UPDOWN</code>, <code>Interface</code>, <code>Gi0/1</code>, <code>changed</code>, <code>state</code>, <code>to</code> na <code>down</code>."

#: syslog_recommendations.php
msgid "An identifier matches when it is <b>exactly equal to one whole word</b>, ignoring case. It is not a \"contains\", \"starts with\" or \"ends with\" search, and there are no wildcards: <code>LINK-3-UPDOWN</code> does not match the word <code>LINK-3-UPDOWN-EXT</code>, and <code>UPDOWN</code> does not match <code>%LINK-3-UPDOWN</code>."
msgstr "Njirimara na-adakọ mgbe ọ <b>ha nhata kpọmkwem na otu okwu zuru oke</b>, n'eleghị anya n'ụdị mkpụrụedemede ukwu ma ọ bụ nta. Ọ bụghị nchọta \"nwere\", \"malite na\" ma ọ bụ \"mechie na\", ọ nweghịkwa wildcard: <code>LINK-3-UPDOWN</code> adabaghị na okwu ahụ <code>LINK-3-UPDOWN-EXT</code>, ma <code>UPDOWN</code> adabaghị na <code>%LINK-3-UPDOWN</code>."

#: syslog_recommendations.php
msgid "A leading <b>%</b> is literal, not a wildcard, and must match the message word as written. An identifier <code>%LINK-3-UPDOWN</code> matches the message word <code>%LINK-3-UPDOWN</code>, not <code>LINK-3-UPDOWN</code>; an identifier without the prefix matches only the unprefixed word."
msgstr "<b>%</b> nke dị n'ihu bụ nke nkịtị, ọ bụghị wildcard, ma ga-adabarịrị na okwu ozi dị ka e dere ya. Ihe njirimara <code>%LINK-3-UPDOWN</code> dabara na okwu ozi <code>%LINK-3-UPDOWN</code>, ọ bụghị <code>LINK-3-UPDOWN</code>; ihe njirimara na-enweghị mbido dabara naanị na okwu na-enweghị mbido."

#: syslog_recommendations.php
msgid "When the syslog host is a Cacti device whose vendor is recognised from its SNMP system description or device template, and recommendations exist for that vendor, only that vendor's recommendations and those without a vendor are checked. Otherwise all vendors are checked, but an identifier made only of digits matches only recommendations without a vendor. When several recommendations match, the longest identifiers are shown first, up to three."
msgstr "Mgbe onye nnabata syslog bụ ngwaọrụ Cacti nke a matara onye na-ere ya site na nkọwa usoro SNMP ya ma ọ bụ nlereanya ngwaọrụ ya, ma ndụmọdụ dị maka onye na-ere ahụ, naanị ndụmọdụ onye na-ere ahụ na ndị na-enweghị onye na-ere ka a na-enyocha. Ma ọ bụghị ya, a na-enyocha ndị na-ere niile, mana njirimara e ji naanị mkpụrụedemede ọnụọgụgụ mee na-adakọ naanị ndụmọdụ na-enweghị onye na-ere. Mgbe ọtụtụ ndụmọdụ dakọtara, a na-egosi njirimara ndị kachasị ogologo na mbụ, ruo atọ."

#: syslog_recommendations.php
msgid "Identifiers that contain other characters, such as the <code>#</code> slot placeholder or the <code>|</code> alternatives in some vendor documentation (for example <code>%ASA|PIX-3-331001</code>), are kept and exported but can never match. Set <b>Can Match</b> to No to list them, and edit them into the exact code, for example <code>%ASA-3-331001</code>."
msgstr "Ihe njirimara nwere mkpụrụedemede ndị ọzọ, dịka ebe njide oghere <code>#</code> ma ọ bụ nhọrọ ndị ọzọ <code>|</code> na akwụkwọ ụfọdụ ndị na-ere (dịka ọmụmaatụ <code>%ASA|PIX-3-331001</code>), ka a na-echekwa ma na-ebupụ mana ha enweghị ike ikwekọ ma ọlị. Tọọ <b>Nwere Ike Ikwekọ</b> ka ọ bụrụ Mba iji depụta ha, ma dezie ha ka ha bụrụ kpọmkwem koodu ahụ, dịka ọmụmaatụ <code>%ASA-3-331001</code>."

